{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791054165,"nonce":"xYHXlWGQe8mgvQegBNoDwiljU6g=","title":"TextMeasureContext drops letter-spacing, so spaced text lays out narrower than it draws","message":"blinc_layout's measurer honours TextLayoutOptions.letter_spacing, and\nthe paint path carries RenderProps.letter_spacing into the drawn glyphs.\nTextMeasureContext had no such field, and neither place in tree.rs that\nbuilds TextLayoutOptions from a context set it. Taffy therefore sized a\nletter-spaced line to its unspaced width.\n\nText already tracks letter_spacing and feeds it to render_props, so its\nown .letter_spacing() modifier hit this too, not just external callers\ndriving the context directly.\n\nNot covered: CSS letter-spacing reaches RenderProps through the\nstylesheet pass, which runs after build() has already made the measure\ncontext. A caller can push it in with LayoutTree::update_text, which is\nhow ashui drives font_size and line_height, but nothing in Blinc wires\nthe CSS value back into the context automatically.\n\nReported by the ashui session; tracked there as 2a1fc12.","files":null}]}